LOK: Calc's selection read counts the cells holding something

ElyTable asks before a merge that would hide more than one cell's
data, and counted the cells from the selection's text. An empty range
has no text at all: getTextSelection fails, so merging empty cells
failed (GitHub ElyOffice #12). .uno:SelectedRange now reports
"filled", the cells in the selected range holding anything.

--- a/sc/source/ui/unoobj/docuno.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/unoobj/docuno.cxx
@@ -1155,6 +1155,12 @@
         rJsonWriter.put("range", aTarget);
         if (aTarget.isEmpty())
             return;
+        // Cells holding anything; an empty range has no text.
+        sal_Int64 nFilled = 0;
+        ScCellIterator aCells(rDoc, aRange);
+        for (bool bHas = aCells.first(); bHas; bHas = aCells.next())
+            ++nFilled;
+        rJsonWriter.put("filled", nFilled);
         // The data inside it: its corners, first row, header guess.
         SCCOL nCol1 = aRange.aStart.Col(), nCol2 = aRange.aEnd.Col();
         SCROW nRow1 = aRange.aStart.Row(), nRow2 = aRange.aEnd.Row();
